{title: Drunken Sailor}
{artist: Traditional}
{album: Sea Shanties}
{meta: language English}
{key: Dm}
{meta: tags shanty, traditional}
{chord_style: trailing}
{copyright: Traditional sea shanty. Public domain.}

{start_of_chorus}
Way hay and up she rises	[Dm]
Way hay and up she rises	[C]
Way hay and up she rises	[Dm]
Early in the morning	[F] [C] [Dm] ([A] [Dm])
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
What will we do with a drunken sailor?	[Dm]
What will we do with a drunken sailor?	[C]
What will we do with a drunken sailor?	[Dm]
Early in the morning	[F] [C] [Dm] ([A7] [Dm])
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Put him in the long boat till he's sober	[Dm] ([Gm])
Put him in the long boat till he's sober	[C] ([F] [C])
Put him in the long boat till he's sober	[Dm]
Early in the morning	[F] [C] [Dm] ([A] [Dm])
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
